 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "energy is the starting energy E; positions[i] and costs[i] describe wall i (positions are distinct and non-zero). Moving costs nothing; every crossing of a wall costs its cost, including crossing the same wall again. Return the largest number of distinct walls that can be crossed with total cost at most E. Any route crosses the nearest i walls on one side and the nearest j on the other; going right first costs 2 R(i) + L(j) and going left first costs R(i) + 2 L(j), where R and L are the summed costs of those walls.",
